  "method": "Derived. Radius 1002.68 m = the sourced circumference 6.3 km / 2 pi (Shiltsev: \"circumference of 6.3 km\"); a circle because the Tevatron shared the Main Ring tunnel and circumference and the MI-60 relation below fits it (no primary source consulted says \"circular\"). Centre from the Main Injector TDR relation quoted in Beams-doc-1148 Appendix A: the MI-60 straight \"is parallel to the Tevatron F0 straight section\", its reference point \"is 13.222 m downstream from the F0 TeV point, and offset from the TeV straight section by 11.823 m\". The MI-60 reference point is the lattice origin of the TDR site-coordinate table (DUSAF x = 101516.842 ft, y = 97134.405 ft, heading 148.76849 deg ccw from site east, i.e. geodetic azimuth 339.5 deg); the F0 point is 13.222 m upstream of it along the heading and 11.823 m to the right (the Main Injector lies south-west of the Tevatron), and the ring centre is a radius further along the right-hand normal. Site coordinates were converted with the FSCS of Beams-doc-1148. Result: centre 41.831643 N, 88.252077 W. Independent test, not used in the placement: the published A0 point (the origin of the site grid, on the Tevatron/Main Ring A0 straight) lies 999.7 m from this centre against the 1002.68 m radius. The earlier placement came from a circle fit to OSM service roads (centre 41.831724 N, 88.251594 W, rms 57 m); it is 41 m from this one. The OSM CDF Hall and D0 Assembly buildings lie 1017.7 m and 1032.1 m from the centre, 15 m and 30 m outside the ring, as surface buildings beside the underground collision halls should; the two distance checks that took them for ring points were removed. Accuracy 10 m: A0 residual 3 m, the 2.7 m between a 1000 m and a 1002.68 m radius, and design versus as-built positions.",
  "name": "Tevatron ring (derived circle, placed from the Main Injector TDR; decommissioned 2011)",
  "notes": [
    "No primary source consulted uses the word 'circular' or states a numeric radius for the Tevatron. The circle is a derived representation: the sourced 6.3 km circumference, in the Main Ring tunnel it shared. Secondary sources describe the ring as circular, but they are not cited here. The shape stays derived.",
    "Re-placed on 2026-10-25 from the Main Injector design handbook's relation and the Fermilab Site Coordinate System; the OpenStreetMap ring-road centre it replaces was 41 m away. A distance check to the A0 point replaces the two hall-centroid checks, which assumed the surface buildings stand on the ring."
  ],
